---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
import CompareTable from '../components/CompareTable.astro';
import Faq from '../components/Faq.astro';
import Cta from '../components/Cta.astro';
import data from '../data/competitors.json';
import { faqPage, itemList } from '../lib/site';

const order = ['Pillar', 'Meetra', 'Saathiya', 'DashTalk', 'Talkie', 'Nomi', 'Kindroid', 'Replika'];
const all = [...data.apps, ...data.global];
const apps = order.map((n) => all.find((a) => a.name === n));
const editorialUpdated = '26 September 2026';
const faq = [
  { q: 'Is there a free alternative to Character AI in India?', a: 'Yes. Pillar, Meetra, Saathiya, DashTalk and Talkie can all be started for free.' },
  { q: 'Which Character AI alternative speaks Hindi?', a: 'Pillar, Meetra, Saathiya and DashTalk are built for Hindi and Hinglish; Pillar and Meetra also list Tamil, Telugu, Marathi, Bengali and more. The global alternatives — Talkie, Nomi, Kindroid, Replika — are English-first.' },
  { q: 'Which alternative has voice calls?', a: 'DashTalk, Meetra, Pillar, Nomi, Kindroid and Replika list voice calls.' },
  { q: 'Which alternatives mention memory?', a: 'Pillar, Meetra, Nomi and Kindroid describe memory features. Try the same companion over several conversations to see whether the experience fits you.' },
];
---
<Base title="Character AI Alternatives in India (2026): 8 Apps Compared" description="Looking for an alternative to Character AI in India? Apps with Hindi and Indian languages, voice calls, memory and romantic conversations — compared, with Pillar included." path="/character-ai-alternatives-india" jsonld={[itemList(order), faqPage(faq)]}>
  <p class="eyebrow">Alternatives · India · 2026</p>
  <h1 style="font-family:var(--font-serif); font-size:clamp(1.9rem, 4.5vw, 2.8rem); line-height:1.15; margin:0.4rem 0 1rem;">Character AI alternatives for Indian users (2026)</h1>
  <div class="answer">
    <p>If you want a ready-made Indian companion who can speak your language and continue a conversation over time, compare <strong>Pillar</strong>, <strong>Meetra</strong>, <strong>Saathiya</strong> and <strong>DashTalk</strong>. If you prefer a wider character library or an English-first experience, consider <strong>Talkie</strong>, <strong>Nomi</strong>, <strong>Kindroid</strong> and <strong>Replika</strong>. Pillar offers more than 100 ready-made companions, voice calls, memory and thirteen named languages.</p>
  </div>
  <p style="color:var(--color-dim); font-size:0.85rem;">Last updated: {editorialUpdated}. Pillar is our app. Our team has tried the compared apps; feature cells for the others describe their linked public Play listings, not a standardised test.</p>

  <section class="prose-pillar">
    <h2>What Character AI does well</h2>
    <p>Character AI centres on a library of user-made characters. If exploring many characters is what you want, that approach may fit better than choosing one companion for an ongoing conversation.</p>
    <h2>When an Indian-language companion may fit better</h2>
    <p>Choose based on the experience you want: a ready-made companion, conversations in an Indian language, voice calls, memory, or messages that arrive first. Pillar combines those choices; the table shows which features other apps mention in their listings.</p>
    <p>In our team's sessions with Meetra and Saathiya, companions replied after we wrote to them, but did not initiate a later message. That is what we observed in those conversations, not a guarantee about every version of either app.</p>
  </section>

  <CompareTable include={order} />

  <section class="prose-pillar">
    {apps.map((a) => (
      <>
        <h2>{a.name} — best if you want {a.bestFor}</h2>
        <p>{a.name === 'Pillar' ? 'Pillar offers more than 100 ready-made companions from Indian cities, thirteen languages, voice notes and calls, photos, memory, games, and companions who can message first. You can begin without giving an email address or phone number; your generated username appears in Profile.' : `Languages on its listing: ${a.cells[0]}.`} <strong>Consideration:</strong> {a.limit}</p>
        {a.play && <p><a href={a.play} rel="noopener nofollow" target="_blank">{a.name} on Google Play →</a></p>}
      </>
    ))}
  </section>

  <section class="prose-pillar">
    <h2>Which alternative for which need</h2>
    <ul>
      <li><strong>Hindi or another Indian language:</strong> Pillar, Meetra, Saathiya, DashTalk.</li>
      <li><strong>One companion with memory, in English:</strong> Nomi, Kindroid, Replika.</li>
      <li><strong>Many characters and roleplay, in English:</strong> Talkie.</li>
      <li><strong>Voice calls in Hindi:</strong> DashTalk, Pillar, Meetra.</li>
    </ul>
  </section>

  <Cta text="Try Pillar — the Indian-language alternative" />
  <Faq items={faq} />
  <section class="prose-pillar"><h2>Related</h2><p><a href="/best-ai-girlfriend-apps-india">Best AI girlfriend apps in India</a> · <a href="/best-ai-companion-apps-india">Best AI companion apps in India</a> · <a href="/ai-companion-apps-with-many-companions">Apps with many companions</a> · <a href="/apps-like-replika-india">Apps like Replika for Indian users</a> · <a href="/hi/ai-girlfriend-hindi">AI girlfriend in Hindi</a></p></section>
</Base>
